      "value": "@{62df7cd83e007e467295c4e1|full_name}: In all honesty, no.\n\n I can understand that you aren't able to view the details of a world that doesn't have a file on the server (Worlds being built on the local machine through VRChat SDK also don't have a file and exibit the same behavior as the Error World).\n\nHowever, in trying this out, one can see something that if not a bug, is a serious design flaw.\n\nA world can cause you to reload without user input, I have the confirm all portals setting so it shouldn't be that I spawned in a portal and activate it immediately.\n\nVRChat's System Account's \"The In-Between\" does this (Repeatedly, as it does this as soon as you join world).\n\nI wanted to document a more serious bug through submitting a potential non-bug that the idea of taking seriously would be humorous.\n\nFurther, Akin to what you suggested, I do think that something along the lines of denying the VRChat Home world even exists in the menu, possibly by having it's details page temporarily replaced with \"Never heard of it\" (or something alike) would be funny for an April fools prank",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
